# Scoped to this directory's `Dockerfile` alone -- BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in
# preference to the context's own `.dockerignore`, so this list never reaches any other tool that
# walks the tree.
#
# The Dockerfile is named `Dockerfile` and not `Dockerfile.nvs`: `.nvs` is the language's own source
# extension, and a build file wearing it reads as a Novis program to every editor, every glob in this
# repository and every person.
#
# The context is the repository root because the build stage compiles the workspace. What that costs
# is entirely decided here: `target/` is tens of gigabytes and `website/node_modules` tens of
# thousands of files, and sending either takes longer than the compile it feeds.

# Build output, on both sides of the mount.
target/
**/target/

# The unattended loop's logs and scratch, neither of which any build reads.
.loop/
.agent-tmp/

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/

# The website and its dependency tree -- not part of the workspace `cargo build` walks.
website/
editors/*/node_modules/

# Fuzzing corpora and artifacts: large, and regenerated rather than compiled.
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/

# The benchmark's own outputs, so a rebuild never carries the previous run in. The staged binary is
# the one exception and the negation is deliberate: the `prebuilt` stage's whole input is that file,
# and an ignore rule matching it would make that stage fail with "file not found" for a file that is
# plainly on disk. Last match wins, so this pair must stay in this order.
benches/*.json
benches/proxied/.bin/
!benches/proxied/.bin/nvs

# Documentation, except the pages the build compiles in: `crates/nvs-stdlib/build.rs` reads the
# `docs/reference/core/` intros, and `crates/nvs-cli/src/agent.rs`
# `include_str!`s the reference chapters. An edit to any other doc must not invalidate the context
# layer and cost a rebuild of everything after it. Last match wins, so the negations stay below.
docs/
*.md
!README.md
!docs/reference/**
